    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T23:36:10Z",
    "body": "local commit 88f489e on issue/152-short-bar-axis (not pushed yet). When the normal moment is isotropic, the fit now also tries the part's flat poles (the facing-flat normals) as candidate axes, and re-centres the line by least trimmed squares when a hole drags it. A sphere and a cube are still refused by name. Pinned by `a_short_punched_bar_reads_as_turned_about_its_axis` (fails on main) plus the `axis_poles` unit tests. `punched_bar` stays at L/D 5: at r10 x 40 the three-hole box fixtures go past the 10 % concurrency share.\n",
